% technique_id: T1218.008
% technique_name: Odbcconf
% domain: enterprise
% tactic(s): defense-evasion
% platforms: Windows
% url: https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1218/008
% is_subtechnique: yes
% stix_id: attack-pattern--6e3bd510-6b33-41a4-af80-2d80f3ee0071
% description: Adversaries may abuse odbcconf.exe to proxy execution of malicious payloads. Odbcconf.exe is a Windows utility that allows you to configure Open Database Connectivity (ODBC) drivers and data source names.(Citation: Microsoft odbcconf.exe) The Odbcconf.exe binary may be digitally signed by Microsoft.  Adversaries may abuse odbcconf.exe to bypass application control solutions that do not account for its potential abuse. Similar to [Regsvr32](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1218/010), odbcconf.exe has a <code>REGSVR</code> flag that can be misused to execute DLLs (ex: <code>odbcconf.exe /S /A {REGSVR "C:\Users\Public\file.dll"}</code>). (Citation: LOLBAS Odbcconf)(Citation: TrendMicro Squiblydoo Aug 2017)(Citation: TrendMicro Cobalt Group Nov 2017)
% generated_by: notebook_generate_rules

% ---- RULE LLM START (minimal) ----
    uses_legitimate_service(Host, odbcconf) :-
        app_installed(Host, odbcconf, _Version),
        attacker_at(net),
        connects(net, Host, _Port).

    bypasses_app_control(Host) :-
        uses_legitimate_service(Host, odbcconf),
        exec(Host, user).

    compromise(Host, user) :-
        bypasses_app_control(Host).
% ---- RULE LLM END ----
